  <section class="sky chapter night" id="sky">
    <div class="sky__visual">
      <img class="parallax" src="/img/projected-calendar.jpeg" alt="A hand touches the illuminated centre of a circular celestial diagram" />
      <div class="orbit orbit--one" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="orbit orbit--two" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <p>Observe · return · remember</p>
    </div>
    <div class="sky__heading reveal"><p>Part one</p><h2>The first clock<br />had no hands.</h2></div>
    <div class="prose prose--narrow reveal">
      <p class="dropcap">Look upward and the earliest instruments are already in motion. The sun makes a path without touching the ground. The moon changes its face. Certain stars disappear into one season and return in another.</p>
      <p>What we call time began as a relationship between bodies: earth and sun, moon and tide, shadow and wall, sleeper and dawn. The sky offered repetition, but never sameness. Each return carried a difference, a colder wind, a fuller river, one more child old enough to ask when.</p>
      <p>Counting was not a retreat from wonder. It was a way of staying close to it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="year-line reveal"><span>solstice</span><i></i><span>equinox</span><i></i><span>solstice</span><i></i><span>equinox</span><i></i></div>
  </section>

  <section class="agreement chapter paper" id="agreement">
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <chapter-marker number="02" label="To count is to choose"></chapter-marker>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
    <header class="agreement__heading reveal"><p>The calendar is not discovered whole.</p><h2>It is a world,<br /><span>chosen.</span></h2></header>
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <editorial-plate class-name="plate--manuscript" src="/img/manuscript.jpeg" alt="An open handwritten manuscript, its pages marked by age" folio="Plate 02" caption="Memory given a surface."></editorial-plate>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
    <aside class="agreement__symbol reveal">
      <img src="/img/material-spiritual.jpeg" alt="A hand-drawn circle and square captioned Material world, spiritual world" />
      <p>A useful calendar holds both: the material world of seasons and the invisible world of meaning.</p>
    </aside>
    <div class="prose agreement__copy reveal">
      <p>There is no neutral way to divide a life. One culture begins the day at midnight, another at sunset. One year follows the sun; another listens to the moon; another keeps both in conversation through careful adjustment.</p>
      <p>These are not errors waiting to become one system. They are different agreements with the cosmos. A calendar reveals which threshold matters: a monsoon, a migration, a ritual, the settling of an account, the remembered birth of a teacher or a god.</p>
      <p>When we inherit a calendar, we inherit its priorities. Workdays and holy days, fiscal quarters and seasons of fasting, birthdays and anniversaries, all are claims upon attention.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cosmos" aria-label="Cosmic interlude">
    <img class="parallax" src="/img/nebula.jpeg" alt="A dark nebula scattered with brilliant stars" />
    <p class="cosmos__caption split">The sky keeps no calendar.<br />We keep one beneath it.</p><span>§</span>
  </section>

  <section class="ritual chapter paper" id="ritual">
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <chapter-marker number="03" label="Ritual time"></chapter-marker>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
    <header class="ritual__heading reveal"><h2>Repetition<br />makes time<br /><span>inhabitable.</span></h2><p>We do not live in units. We live in returns.</p></header>
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <editorial-plate class-name="plate--ritual" src="/img/ritual-bathing.jpeg" alt="Detail of a historical painting showing figures bathing among lotus flowers" folio="Plate 03" caption="Water, gesture, return."></editorial-plate>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
    <div class="prose ritual__copy reveal">
      <p>Ritual takes an abstract interval and gives it weight. A lamp is lit. Water is poured. A name is spoken again. The gesture may last only a minute, yet because it has been performed before, and will be performed after, it holds more than the present.</p>
      <p>This is how a date becomes a day. The recurring act binds private memory to collective rhythm. It gives grief somewhere to return, gratitude a form, and anticipation a horizon.</p>
      <p>A calendar without ritual is only a ledger. Ritual turns the ledger into a dwelling.</p>
    </div>
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <editorial-plate class-name="plate--silence float" src="/img/silent-area.jpeg" alt="A wooden sign in dense greenery reads Silent Area" folio="Marginalia" caption="A pause is also an interval."></editorial-plate>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
  </section>

  <section class="ledger chapter" id="ledger">
    <header class="ledger__heading reveal"><p>Part four · the measured self</p><h2>When every hour<br />must explain itself.</h2></header>
    <div class="prose prose--narrow ledger__copy reveal">
      <p class="dropcap">Modern time arrives pre-divided. It vibrates in a pocket, colours a meeting block, counts the sleep beneath our eyelids and asks whether the morning was productive.</p>
      <p>The clock gives coordination, but it also creates a peculiar guilt: the feeling that an unclaimed hour has been wasted. We begin to speak about time as if it were a substance leaking from a damaged vessel, spent, saved, borrowed, lost.</p>
      <p>But not every hour needs an outcome. Some hours ripen invisibly. Some are devoted to looking, waiting, grieving, wandering, or doing nothing that can be entered in a field.</p>
    </div>
    {% renderTemplate "webc" %}
      <editorial-plate class-name="plate--metal" src="/img/hour-revenge.jpeg" alt="An oval metal plaque engraved with the words The hour is devoted to revenge" folio="Found instruction" caption="Taken literally at our peril."></editorial-plate>
      <editorial-plate class-name="plate--future" src="/img/future-self.jpeg" alt="A folded note reads Do something today that your future self will thank you for" folio="Found instruction" caption="Even the future becomes a creditor."></editorial-plate>
    {% endrenderTemplate %}
    <p class="ledger__number" aria-hidden="true">24</p>
  </section>

  <section class="proposition paper">
    <p class="proposition__label reveal">A small proposition</p>
    <blockquote class="split">Let the calendar be a trellis, not a cage.</blockquote>
    <div class="prose reveal"><p>Use it to hold what matters upright: the people who return, the seasons worth noticing, the work that asks for patience, the ceremonies that make a community visible to itself.</p><p>Leave some squares unclaimed. The unknown is not empty time. It is where attention can change direction.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="rings" id="rings">
    <figure><img src="/img/tree-time.jpeg" alt="A large old tree with a reflection about a tree born on the same day as you" /></figure>
    <div class="rings__copy reveal"><p>Part five · after the date</p><h2>What grows<br />beside us.</h2><p>Somewhere, a tree may have begun on the day you did. It has not counted the years. It has made rings from weather: abundance, injury, drought, recovery. Its calendar is held inside the body.</p><p>Perhaps ours is too. We carry years in posture, memory, skill, scar, tenderness. The date is only the doorplate. Time is the room we have made behind it.</p></div>
  </section>

